{
  "$comment": "Verifier's expected closed configuration (build spec §6 correction 20; D1 A.9; Review B17; E18). Durations are integer seconds unless `unit` says otherwise. `fixed` keys accept only their default. Tests read expectations from this file, never from the engine. M2 (SEAM.md §115) adds the engine and project keys of D2 A.7, byte-valued keys in bytes (2 GiB = 2147483648): `ui_bootstrap` is false in qualified M2 (K3); `budget_hard_maximum` is a boolean whose value true is refused with `hard_cap_unenforceable`, not `invalid_value`; `budget_run_boundary` takes a BudgetBoundary; `egress_allow_extra` and `sandbox_read_paths` are widenings (`policy_widening`); the backend keys name the backend each role is dispatched to and the mode, as SEAM.md §116 says. M3 slice 15 (D3 A.7; SEAM.md §186) adds the check runner's engine keys `check_timeout_max`, `check_output_max_bytes`, `checktree_max_bytes`, `checktree_max_entries`, `checktrees_max_bytes` and `check_infra_retries_max`, and the project key `max_concurrent_checks` (not a widening). `checktrees_max_bytes` has a second lower bound, `at_least`: it may not be below the effective `checktree_max_bytes`, and its `min` is the lowest value that bound can take. M3 slice 19 (D3 A.7, §3.3; Q5; SEAM.md §217) adds `classifier_authority`, an object `{mode, version?}`: `mode` a ClassifierAuthority (`recommend` or `authoritative`), `version` a positive integer that `authoritative` requires and `recommend` does not take; M07 compares values with `assert.deepEqual`. M4 slice 23 (D4 A.7; BS4 §11.3 as Sean approved it, E121 item 3; SEAM.md §252) adds the deployment engine keys `adapter_effect_deadline`, `adapter_read_deadline`, `adapter_output_max_bytes`, `artifact_max_entries`, `artifact_max_bytes`, `artifacts_max_bytes` (its `at_least` the effective `artifact_max_bytes`), `artifact_prepare_deadline` and the four `service_link_*` keys (D2's `egress_*` defaults and ranges), and the project keys `deploy_orchestration_deadline`, `deploy_auto_retries_max`, `identity_observation_every` and the five `service_*` limits of Q6. M5 slice 31 (D6 K3, K9; A.7; E139 Q3, Q5; SEAM.md §348) adds the project keys `autonomy` (`step`, `stage`, `phase`; default `phase`) and `alpha_deploy` (`manual`, `on_phase_complete`; default `manual`), and raises `max_chained_roles` to a default of 24 within 1 to 64 (a bound on inherited chain depth, not a budget, N02). The session, memory and adoption keys of A.7 are slices 33, 37 and 32's. M5 slice 33 (D6 A.7; E139 Q6; SEAM.md §391) adds the project keys `backend_vision` and `backend_spec_writer` (as the other `backend_*`) and the six `model_<role>` keys, each a model the role's backend entry offers: `opus` for Vision, Spec Writer and Architect, `sonnet` for Builder, Verifier and Reviewer (Claude Code's model aliases). Objection 077 (D6 A.7): the engine key `turn_max_bytes` (64 KiB, 4 KiB to 1 MiB) and the project keys `transcript_max_bytes` (8 MiB, 1 to 64 MiB), `deadline_vision` and `deadline_spec_writer` (30 m, 5 to 180 m). M5 slice 32 (D6 A.7; E140 N4; SEAM.md §377) adds the engine key `adoption_full_max_files` (2,000 within 100 to 100,000; a recommendation on `adoption_mode`, never the choice). M5 slice 35 (D6 §5.2, A.7; the driver's rulings of 2026-10-13; SEAM.md §406) adds the project key `phase_size`, an object `{min, max}`, default `{min 3, max 5}`, each 1 to 12: a plan whose stage count is outside it is routed `uncertain` (`phase_size: …`), never refused. M5 slice 37 (D6 K2, A.7; E140 N1, N2; B09; SEAM.md §437): the engine key `max_concurrent_runs` and the project key `max_concurrent_runs` are removed (each refused as a setting: at start, `unknown_field` naming it; at the policy route, `unknown_field`); `max_concurrent_domains` defaults to 4; the project keys `role_memory_max` (4 GiB) and `check_memory_max` (2 GiB) are added, each from 512 MiB to the engine's `domain_memory_max` (`max` names that key: the effective value is min(the project's value or default, `domain_memory_max`), and an explicit project value above the ceiling is refused 400 `invalid_value`). M6 slice 40 (D7 §2, A.7; BS6 §11.1; E156 Q4: trial values; objection 165; SEAM.md §§491, 499, 516) adds D7 A.7's fifteen project keys at A.7's defaults and ranges, durations in seconds and sizes in bytes: `design` (`off`, `before_build`, `at_alpha`, `both`; default `off`), `design_preview` (default `static`; `off` and `static` allowed, `stack` refused `invalid_value` in M6, E156 Q4), `design_widths` (a list of 1 to 6 widths, each 240 to 3840 px; default [360, 720, 1280]), `design_orientations` (a non-empty subset of `portrait`, `landscape`; default both), `design_external_urls` (host names; default cdn.jsdelivr.net, unpkg.com, cdnjs.cloudflare.com, in that order), `assets_required_for` (`none`, `beta`, `live`, never `alpha`; default `live`), `model_designer` (`opus`, as `model_architect`), `deadline_designer` (30 m within 5 to 180 m), `designer_session_budget_billable_tokens` (3,000,000 within 250,000 to 20,000,000), `design_tree_max_bytes` (32 MiB within 1 to 128 MiB), `design_tree_max_files` (800 within 50 to 8,000), `preview_memory_max` (256 MiB from 64 MiB to the engine's `domain_memory_max`, as `role_memory_max`: `max` names that key), `design_preview_ttl` (24 h within 1 h to 14 d), `design_due_max_defer` (7 d within 1 h to 30 d) and `design_review_evidence_max_bytes` (64 MiB per file within 1 MiB to 2 GiB); and `backend_designer`, the Designer's backend selector as every `backend_<role>` (SEAM.md §391's pattern; not in A.7's table; upheld with objection 165). Slices 41 to 44 read these keys and add none. M6 slice 45 (D7 A.7's '512 MiB per review'; SEAM.md §§522, 536; objection 193) adds the project key `design_review_evidence_max_review_bytes`, the per-review bound: 512 MiB within 1 MiB to 16 GiB (A.7 leaves the range open; the range is the Builder's, accepted by the driver).",
